1
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:12,960
Brighten it up,
then step back and take a look.

2
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:28,640
an afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out.

3
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:35,320
walking while looking back,
holding Gā-chan's hand.

4
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:42,460
that strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:47,740
So on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:53,560
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,680
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,840
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:05,800
Politicians with their self-important faces,

10
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:09,100
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

11
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:12,100
Try turning a corner.

12
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,700
Around that corner

13
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:19,900
I can meet everyone, everyone

14
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:24,540
Over there, there's a wall

15
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:27,820
Surely there's a wall

16
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:33,080
Everyone, come to our town

17
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:34,620
Thank you

18
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:40,720
The boundless, endlessly expanding universe

19
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:45,940
it is said that unknown
intelligent life forms exist there

20
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:48,980
No, perhaps they

21
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:52,860
may already be right beside us

22
00:01:55,420 --> 00:01:56,680
Time, stop

23
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:04,900
At last, the day we've been waiting for

24
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:05,400
Let's go!

25
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,920
Go where, Ryotsu?

26
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:15,820
On patrol, Chief.

27
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:20,300
What's this circle? What's this circle?

28
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:22,560
It's nothing, Chief.

29
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:26,740
Weren't you going to buy a game, Ryotsu?

30
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:29,300
A game?

31
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:31,980
Oh no, did I say something I shouldn't have?

32
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:39,420
Please let me go, Chief.

33
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:43,120
Today's the day we've been waiting for:
the release of Doikura Waibu!

34
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:46,580
Idiot! What are you
babbling about while on duty?

35
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:49,240
Do you understand your
position as a police officer?

36
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:50,900
I do.

37
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:52,000
I do understand.

38
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,320
Didn't I hold back from lining up in front of the
shop all night and work the night shift instead?

39
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:03,120
Don't be so stubborn!
Please, I'll be back in 30 seconds, Boochar.

40
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:12,340
We're here too, so I don't think it'd be a problem if you stepped out for a bit.
If it's the shop by the station, you can get there in no time on your bike, right, Ryo-chan?

41
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:17,440
I'm pretty sure your shift ends at noon,
doesn't it, Ryotsu?

42
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:20,560
Yes, Chief. Rotation time is in two minutes.

43
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:24,380
If I wait until my shift is over,
I won't know if I can leave.

44
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:26,900
Well, just do your duty properly.

45
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:27,380
Yes.

46
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:31,120
I'm telling you to keep
working your shift diligently.

47
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,840
Chief, you're so mean.

48
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,080
Ow

49
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:45,940
What? What is it?

50
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:54,580
Everyone, is something

51
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:57,560
Reiko, Nakagawa

52
00:03:58,580 --> 00:03:59,380
Terai

53
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:01,420
Chief

54
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:05,620
It's frozen solid.

55
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:08,100
What on earth is going on?

56
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:10,420
We've figured out the
cause of the malfunction, ya.

57
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:12,620
Looks like we're out of fuel after all.

58
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:13,760
Well, this is a pain, ya.

59
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:16,940
The nearest gas station is
still three light-years away, ya.

60
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:21,880
We stopped off for a drink,
and now we've run short on fuel

61
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:24,500
You were happily drinking too, ya.

62
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,500
What are you all doing?

63
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:31,100
Crushed

64
00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:32,280
Sorry.

65
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:36,340
That's awful.

66
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:39,640
What the heck is this thing?

67
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:42,580
So this is what caused that shaking earlier?

68
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:45,620
Where'd you haul in such
a huge sake barrel from?

69
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:46,520
Stop it!

70
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:49,140
It's a spaceship, dammit!

71
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:53,300
A spaceship?
This is a spaceship, you lot are the aliens!

72
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:59,380
What's alien about those outfits that
make you look like a failing comedy duo?

73
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:00,420
Hey!

74
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:05,920
Aliens look like this, you know.

75
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:10,420
Gehehehe, there's no such alien!

76
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:14,910
But we stopped all movement on
Earth with the time-stop device,

77
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:16,880
so why is this guy the only one moving?

78
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:18,820
Time-stop device?

79
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:23,320
So you two are responsible for this?

80
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:27,580
We couldn't let anyone see our true forms,
so we stopped time.

81
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:31,540
So you two really are aliens?

82
00:05:32,140 --> 00:05:34,220
That's what we've been saying all along.

83
00:05:34,340 --> 00:05:36,660
Being told that by you really pisses me off.

84
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:37,820
That hurts.

85
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,360
So the fuel data came up, didn't it.

86
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:45,180
Is the fuel in this sake barrel?

87
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,480
This isn't a sake barrel, it's a spaceship!

88
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:49,140
I already said I get it, geez.

89
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,940
Why isn't it in Japanese

90
00:05:52,940 --> 00:05:56,000
Beer, sake, shochu, whiskey.

91
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:00,100
Mozuku, hokke, moro-kyu,
chicken wings, daikon salad.

92
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:02,560
This is an izakaya menu, isn't it!

93
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:07,840
With the ingredients on that list, we should be able
to make something nearly identical to the real fuel.

94
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:14,020
If you help us, we'll set off right away
and get the stopped time moving again.

95
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:18,120
Wait, does that mean time has stopped?

96
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,680
The game hasn't come out yet.

97
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:27,920
Alright, I'll cooperate with you.

98
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:35,880
It's like looking at a life-size diorama.

99
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,740
So where's the fuel, then?

100
00:06:39,460 --> 00:06:43,440
There's a regular shop up ahead, so we
should be able to get everything there.

101
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:45,620
Watch out!

102
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:52,660
The cars are stopped too,
so it's fine, dakki.

103
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:55,360
As soon as time starts moving again,
we'll get run over, won't we?

104
00:06:58,640 --> 00:06:59,760
What is this guy?

105
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,900
Did he fall out of his afro?

106
00:07:04,940 --> 00:07:06,080
I'll save you now.

107
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:11,620
Moving something frozen in midair changes the future,
so the Time Law forbids it, nora.

108
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:13,080
How could I just leave him be?

109
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:15,820
Don't you aliens have ninjas or anything?

110
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:17,540
Damn, it won't budge.

111
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:21,680
Things stopped in midair can't
be moved as they are, dakki.

112
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:24,060
You two, come with me.

113
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,620
So this is hokke, is it?

114
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:30,600
No, this is a futon!

115
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,740
You two, stack on top too!

116
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:42,880
Where's the Morokyu, dakki?

117
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,580
There was that Morokyu

118
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:49,720
This bastard,
skipping class in broad daylight!

119
00:07:52,140 --> 00:07:54,160
So that's the Morokyu, dakki. I see.

120
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:57,000
No, like this!

121
00:07:57,540 --> 00:08:00,440
You guys help too.
What is it this time, nano na?

122
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:05,140
This isn't a Morokyu either!

123
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:08,460
Hurry up and take me somewhere I can get some sleep,
will you?

124
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:11,358
You know, on Earth,

125
00:08:11,408 --> 00:08:14,800
there's a saying: those who don't work,
don't eat.

126
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:18,800
There, that's good.

127
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:22,700
If we leave it like this, we'll catch them
right away when they start moving again.

128
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:26,060
Are we going to make another detour?

129
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:27,300
It's impossible.

130
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:29,780
Shut up! A kid is drowning, you know!

131
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:34,000
Damn it, no good,
the water's completely frozen solid.

132
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,400
In that case,

133
00:08:38,420 --> 00:08:40,060
for now, it's first aid.

134
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:41,520
You're really thorough, aren't you.

135
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:42,200
While we're at it,

136
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,220
Here's a bonus.

137
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:50,960
I brought a coach from
the swimming school nearby!

138
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,840
Keep this one close by,

139
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:56,020
if we keep it this secure,
it should be fine.

140
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:03,780
So that's everything on the list now.

141
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:06,100
Good thing it's before opening.

142
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:08,232
Now we can keep our journey going, nora.

143
00:09:08,282 --> 00:09:10,800
We got to meet nice humans, didn't we?

144
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:15,100
Hey, pay up before you go.

145
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,500
We don't have anything like that, ikki.

146
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:17,320
What?

147
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:22,460
We're in the middle of an intergalactic trip that
relies only on everyone's love and kindness, nora.

148
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:26,860
Geez, fine.
Hey, old man, how much is it all together?

149
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:32,480
Look at that carefree face.
I'm leaving the money right here.

150
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:37,760
We put everything in, nodayo.

151
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:39,260
Now we stop it, kki.

152
00:09:39,260 --> 00:09:41,540
We've been helped a lot, kki.

153
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:43,380
We won't forget this kindness, nodayo.

154
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:44,660
You can forget the kindness, but

155
00:09:44,660 --> 00:09:48,180
the money you fronted earlier, when you get promoted
you'd better come back and pay it back double, you hear?

156
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:49,700
Got it, kki.

157
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:53,420
And only restart time after I say it's okay,
you hear?

158
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:59,340
You really got in my way earlier, Chief.

159
00:10:00,340 --> 00:10:01,060
Yo-tto.

160
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:05,380
Yeah, that's about it.

161
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:10,160
I'll let it slide at this much.

162
00:10:22,380 --> 00:10:25,380
Even seeing it fly off in person,
I still can't believe it.

163
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:27,120
Anyway, let's hurry.

164
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:28,460
It worked out, kki.

165
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:30,960
Where's that kind person?

166
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:32,920
Over there, kki.

167
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:41,640
OK, nora.

168
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:42,260
Alright.

169
00:10:55,820 --> 00:10:58,300
Help!

170
00:10:58,300 --> 00:10:59,480
Help!

171
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:01,060
Going outside is too much! Aden!

172
00:11:01,820 --> 00:11:04,100
W-what's happening?!

173
00:11:10,660 --> 00:11:14,367
All that's left is to wait
for the ten o'clock opening.

174
00:11:14,417 --> 00:11:15,920
I wonder what the Chief
is doing right now...

175
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:22,360
It's a misunderstanding!

176
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:30,100
The delivery's...

177
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:38,320
Is the delivery not here yet?

178
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:40,340
Looks like it's not yet.

179
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:42,940
I can't believe they can conduct
an interrogation without a license.

180
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:45,220
Sorry.

181
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:51,300
Yeah, it's me.

182
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:53,820
I don't think I can get away today.

183
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:57,660
You said it'd only take
thirty seconds at most!

184
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:01,120
About that license renewal...

185
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:08,840
Dad, you're not really Dad, are you?

186
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:10,980
Masayoshi.

187
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:15,400
Wait, Dad,
where have you been all this time?

188
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:20,880
Dad, Mom and Grandma have been worried sick.

189
00:12:21,300 --> 00:12:24,300
Aaaaah!

190
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:26,640
Aaaaah!

191
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:26,920
Aaaaah!

192
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:40,800
Yes!

193
00:12:42,060 --> 00:12:42,640
Yes!

194
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:53,600
Hey! I was the first one to make him cry!

195
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:57,520
Damn it! I won't lose, I won't lose!

196
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:01,800
Mister, how much?

197
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:04,360
Sold out. Sorry about that.

198
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:05,480
No way!

199
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,900
No way!

200
00:13:09,140 --> 00:13:11,880
I'll never forget this, you hear!

201
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:12,820
Shut up!

202
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:35,400
When do you feel happiest?

203
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:38,360
When you're eating something delicious.

204
00:13:39,020 --> 00:13:41,840
When you accomplish something
through study or work.

205
00:13:42,820 --> 00:13:45,200
Moments spent with family or a lover.

206
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:49,340
This is the story of a
man named Ryotsu Kankichi,

207
00:13:49,340 --> 00:13:51,028
who

208
00:13:51,078 --> 00:13:55,300
comes across such small, small happiness.

209
00:13:57,660 --> 00:13:59,400
Shit, shit, shit!

210
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:03,300
Nothing good's happened lately

211
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:07,340
I keep losing at the horse races,

212
00:14:07,340 --> 00:14:08,940
Damn it!

213
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:09,380
Aaaahhhh!

214
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:12,680
and the pachinko won't pay out either.

215
00:14:16,400 --> 00:14:18,620
What the hell,
no matter how much it sucks in...

216
00:14:18,620 --> 00:14:21,520
I've got no money, but I'm still hungry.

217
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:39,080
Ryo-san, that milk's old, you know.

218
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:41,620
Say that sort of thing sooner!

219
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:44,840
I think it's yogurt, though.

220
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:49,580
Are you all right, senpai?

221
00:14:49,580 --> 00:14:51,140
Don't set things down on the floor.

222
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:53,900
Biscuits

223
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:55,760
These are Reiko's, aren't they?

224
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:58,360
Right, I'll have these to
tide me over until lunch.

225
00:15:01,220 --> 00:15:05,060
If you eat them without asking,
Reiko-san will scold you, Ryo-san.

226
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:08,200
Not bad at all.

227
00:15:08,940 --> 00:15:10,020
I'm home~

228
00:15:10,540 --> 00:15:13,120
Ryo-chan, you don't think that's...?

229
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:15,160
Yeah, the rich folks
said not to be so stingy.

230
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:17,480
These biscuits are pretty good, you know.

231
00:15:18,140 --> 00:15:20,380
That's a laxative for pets, Ryo-chan.

232
00:15:21,800 --> 00:15:22,740
Wh-what?

233
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:23,820
Ugh...

234
00:15:25,140 --> 00:15:26,200
Aaah!

235
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:28,280
Why would something like that be here?

236
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:32,780
My cat's a little constipated, so I bought
those at a pet shop on my way here this morning.

237
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:34,040
It's empty!

238
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:38,480
You should've known I might eat it
if you left it lying around like that.

239
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:42,920
You're not a baby. You should be able to tell
for yourself whether something's okay to eat.

240
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:49,320
Between the milk earlier and you putting everything in your mouth without checking what's inside,
Ryo-san, the problem is with you.

241
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,520
No way...

242
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:52,760
Are you okay, Ryo-chan?

243
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:01,580
Here it comes!

244
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:06,100
Nakagawa,
go buy some diarrhea medicine and a bento!

245
00:16:06,440 --> 00:16:07,920
A bento?

246
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:10,060
Just hurry up and go!

247
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:10,780
Yes!

248
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:12,140
Ryo-chan.

249
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:15,240
This is the end.

250
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:32,520
Taking that much medicine at
once is bad for your body, senpai.

251
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:35,320
You should really see a doctor, Ryo-chan.

252
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:38,100
To have eaten too many pet
laxatives because you were hungry...

253
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:40,260
I'm too embarrassed to say it,
but Nakagawa, the bento!

254
00:16:40,260 --> 00:16:42,700
You shouldn't force yourself to eat, senpai.

255
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:43,920
That's right, Ryo-san.

256
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:45,120
Just hand it over.

257
00:16:45,620 --> 00:16:48,460
You should eat plenty while
you still have the strength.

258
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:55,140
Senpai.

259
00:16:55,140 --> 00:16:56,100
Ryo-chan.

260
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:14,240
You look pale, senpai.

261
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:16,520
I've been to the toilet ten times already!

262
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:17,820
Well, of course.

263
00:17:18,380 --> 00:17:21,360
You forced yourself to eat,
so of course it keeps coming out, senpai.

264
00:17:21,360 --> 00:17:22,360
Do you think so?

265
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:26,080
I thought I'd lose all my strength
if it just kept coming out.

266
00:17:26,080 --> 00:17:29,340
Maybe my theory was wrong.

267
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,640
Ryo-chan, you should drink some fluids.

268
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:34,020
It's coming again!

269
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:37,360
Stimulating it like this is bad.

270
00:17:38,220 --> 00:17:38,960
Ryo-chan.

271
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:45,980
In my state right now, even the
slightest stimulation could be fatal!

272
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,500
Sorry, my hand slipped.

273
00:17:48,580 --> 00:17:50,580
If you open it all the way,
I'll knock you flying.

274
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:56,020
What is it now?

275
00:17:57,020 --> 00:17:57,700
Look at that.

276
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:00,980
Senpai, the water's been cut off!

277
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:02,160
Water's been cut off?

278
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:07,060
Oh no! We got a notice that the water pipe work starts at 1 p.m. today!
I forgot!

279
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:11,400
It just passed 1 o'clock!
We can't use the toilet anymore!

280
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:13,160
Ryo-chan...

281
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:14,951
What...

282
00:18:15,001 --> 00:18:20,000
There should still be some
water left in the toilet tank...

283
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:26,600
Terao-kisama!

284
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:30,040
The water's cut off starting at 1 PM.

285
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:33,640
The water Terai-san just
flushed was the last cup.

286
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:36,100
Sorry, Ryo-san.

287
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:39,120
I've been holding it in too, you know.

288
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:42,520
The water cutoff lasts

289
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:43,780
three hours.

290
00:18:43,780 --> 00:18:45,500
Hurry, hurry, hurry, time's up!

291
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:47,820
Ryo-chan

292
00:18:47,820 --> 00:18:48,680
Senpai

293
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:49,660
Ryo-san

294
00:18:51,180 --> 00:18:52,620
The police box is here.

295
00:18:52,620 --> 00:18:56,500
And the area currently
without water is here.

296
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:59,540
We have no choice but to
leave the water-cut area.

297
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:02,700
If we go to the 3-chome police box,
we can borrow the toilet.

298
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:05,900
That's about 500 meters in a straight line.

299
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:08,500
I'll drive you, senpai.

300
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:12,440
No way.
I can't even sit in a seat, let alone

301
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:17,020
I react so sensitively to even
the faintest vibration of the car.

302
00:19:17,020 --> 00:19:19,580
Walking myself is better.

303
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,600
Be careful, Ryo-chan.

304
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:28,240
Yeah.

305
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:33,200
It's like I'm carrying a nitro bomb.

306
00:19:34,140 --> 00:19:35,300
Yo-you guys.

307
00:19:36,620 --> 00:19:39,020
Since you're good kids,
let's walk along the edge of the road.

308
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:39,960
Yes.

309
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:43,591
Senpai, up ahead,

310
00:19:43,641 --> 00:19:46,940
about 30 meters away, a group of
elementary schoolers is approaching.

311
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:48,500
Get yourself mentally prepared.

312
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:51,580
Their movements are unpredictable.

313
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:52,640
Yes.

314
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:12,960
This isn't it.

315
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:17,040
A dump truck is approaching,
a few dozen meters behind us!

316
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:18,560
Be wary of the vibrations.

317
00:20:20,100 --> 00:20:23,760
Watch out for the vibrations,
I'm telling you!

318
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:30,900
We're safe, somehow.

319
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:31,720
Senpai!

320
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:33,800
Yeah, this time

321
00:20:34,260 --> 00:20:36,460
Ringo is heading your way!

322
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:38,760
Why at a time like this?

323
00:20:38,760 --> 00:20:41,640
Hyah, hyah, hyah!

324
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:44,720
Iida, if we keep on at this pace,

325
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:46,340
Ryo-san, above!

326
00:20:46,340 --> 00:20:47,000
No, no,

327
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:50,380
no, no,

328
00:20:50,380 --> 00:20:51,280
no, no,

329
00:20:52,340 --> 00:20:54,880
Senpai, this time it's definitely the wife.

330
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:55,680
What?

331
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:58,040
Good wind.

332
00:20:58,040 --> 00:21:00,140
Dashi, you know.

333
00:21:00,140 --> 00:21:01,600
It's a desperate situation.

334
00:21:05,380 --> 00:21:06,900
Too close!

335
00:21:10,780 --> 00:21:13,100
Thank you for your cooperation.

336
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:26,100
Okay, a little more,
just a bit more effort, and... there!

337
00:21:36,020 --> 00:21:37,600
W-we're on patrol!

338
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:39,200
N-no way!

339
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:42,080
Damn, it's no good, it's locked!

340
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:45,760
Senpai!

341
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:50,760
I'm losing my mind.

342
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:54,540
- Let's find a house that might let us use its toilet!
- Yes!

343
00:21:56,280 --> 00:22:00,100
Toilet... toilet...

344
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:03,780
- Excuse me!
- Hello!

345
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:07,460
Hello!

346
00:22:10,080 --> 00:22:11,963
Toilet...

347
00:22:12,013 --> 00:22:15,880
Toilet... toilet...

348
00:22:15,880 --> 00:22:20,120
Toilet!

349
00:22:20,120 --> 00:22:22,100
Hurry!

350
00:22:22,320 --> 00:22:23,420
Let go!

351
00:22:23,540 --> 00:22:24,080
Hurry!

352
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:32,460
Found it!

353
00:22:36,620 --> 00:22:38,480
Move!

354
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:43,700
Don't come near!

355
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:47,920
Hurry!

356
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:58,300
Ngggggggggggggggggggg

357
00:22:58,300 --> 00:22:58,960
Ugh!

358
00:23:01,300 --> 00:23:04,380
Get out of the way!

359
00:23:08,300 --> 00:23:09,140
Ugh...

360
00:23:09,140 --> 00:23:09,360
Ugh...

361
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:10,660
Ryo-san!

362
00:23:10,940 --> 00:23:11,460
Senpai!

363
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:14,000
No, it's finally... ugh!

364
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:15,680
Ugh...

365
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:16,200
Ugh...

366
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:17,000
Ugh...

367
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,800
You, help!

368
00:23:18,900 --> 00:23:20,060
Ugh...

369
00:23:20,060 --> 00:23:50,040
Nngggghhhh...

370
00:24:03,760 --> 00:24:04,500
Terary

371
00:24:04,500 --> 00:24:05,980
Apparently you built your own home.

372
00:24:05,980 --> 00:24:06,860
That's great.

373
00:24:06,860 --> 00:24:07,920
So where is it?

374
00:24:08,340 --> 00:24:09,400
Do we have to cross a border?

375
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:10,260
No idea.

376
00:24:10,260 --> 00:24:12,400
What? Can't we come by car?

377
00:24:12,860 --> 00:24:13,220
Hey.

378
00:24:13,220 --> 00:24:15,480
Where on earth is your house?

379
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:16,340
Next time

380
00:24:16,340 --> 00:24:17,920
Faraway Terary Prefecture

381
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:18,840
See you then.

382
00:24:20,060 --> 00:24:22,800
Thanks for watching.

